WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.860
Some systems are too tangled to reason about in words.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.800
Two feedback loops, a delay, or a crowd of competing cells can behave in ways

3
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.660
intuition does not predict.

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.700
And a measured curve cannot say why it has its shape.

5
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.540
A model proposes a cause, and makes a number that the cause must produce.

6
00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:31.363
First, state the assumptions, including what is left out.

7
00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:36.403
The classical predator-prey model assumes prey grow exponentially without

8
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:40.563
predators. Consumption is proportional to prey times predators.

9
00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:42.583
There is no handling time.

10
00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.443
And each predator dies at a constant rate.

11
00:00:46.233 --> 00:00:49.333
Second, write the rules as an equation.

12
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:54.713
Exponential growth is dN by dt equals rN.

13
00:00:55.573 --> 00:01:02.913
Logistic growth is rN times 1 minus N over K. Growth per individual falls in a

14
00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:11.473
straight line with N. Total growth peaks at half of K. And K is an equilibrium, not a ceiling.

15
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:18.903
Third, run it. The predator-prey equations give repeating cycles that neither grow

16
00:01:18.903 --> 00:01:22.903
nor shrink, with predator peaks lagging prey peaks.

17
00:01:23.963 --> 00:01:27.063
Now change one assumption and run it again.

18
00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:30.983
Make prey growth logistic, and the cycles change.

19
00:01:32.023 --> 00:01:35.183
Check which conclusions survive a changed assumption.

20
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:40.187
Then compare with data the model was not fitted to.

21
00:01:41.007 --> 00:01:45.207
Hodgkin and Huxley fitted their squid axon model to separate current measurements.

22
00:01:46.087 --> 00:01:52.567
For one fibre at 18.5 degrees Celsius, the 1952 equations predicted conduction at

23
00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.447
18.8 metres a second.

24
00:01:55.207 --> 00:01:57.627
The measurement was 21.2.

25
00:01:58.527 --> 00:02:03.307
Study that gap. Where a model fails shows what to test next.

26
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.600
A fit is not a mechanism.

27
00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:11.460
Several curves with different assumptions can fit the same points.

28
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.180
Hodgkin and Huxley's n⁴ was a fit to data, not a count of channel

29
00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.400
parts. So test predictions and assumptions, not fit alone.

30
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:29.600
And competitive exclusion is predicted with one limiting resource, a constant

31
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.380
environment, and no other check on the winner.

32
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.080
List the conditions with the conclusion.

33
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:41.283
The Hodgkin and Huxley equations of 1952 described the currents.

34
00:02:41.903 --> 00:02:43.883
They did not prove a gating mechanism.

35
00:02:44.903 --> 00:02:49.623
The conductance model of squid axon computed the action potential and the conduction

36
00:02:49.623 --> 00:02:54.663
speed, and a historical review credits it with predicting features of channel gating

37
00:02:54.663 --> 00:02:56.423
before channels could be seen.

38
00:02:57.603 --> 00:03:01.523
In the 1930s, Gause grew two Paramecium species.

39
00:03:02.263 --> 00:03:05.023
Alone, each followed roughly logistic curves.

40
00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:10.123
Mixed, aurelia persisted and caudatum declined in his cultures.

41
00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:14.363
It was a laboratory test of the Lotka-Volterra theory of competition.

42
00:03:15.283 --> 00:03:21.603
In 1996, Huang and Ferrell solved the rate equations of the MAPK cascade.

43
00:03:22.503 --> 00:03:28.043
The model predicted ultrasensitivity, a Hill coefficient of 4 to 5, though no

44
00:03:28.043 --> 00:03:31.883
cooperative enzyme was assumed. Oocyte extracts matched.

45
00:03:32.703 --> 00:03:38.363
In 2008, Deppmann and colleagues simulated neurons competing for NGF made at a

46
00:03:38.363 --> 00:03:44.563
constant rate. Neurons separated into winners and losers only with feedback on TrkA

47
00:03:44.563 --> 00:03:46.263
level and on signal duration.

48
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:49.063
The predictions were tested in mouse ganglia.

49
00:03:49.923 --> 00:03:55.303
Keep this rule. A good fit does not show that the equation's mechanism is the one at work.
